Feature <code>switch</code> <code>match</code> Comparison Type Loose (<code>==</code>) Strict (<code>===</code>) Return Mechanism Statement (requires manual variable assignment) Expression (returns a value directly) Fall-through Requires explicit <code>break;</code> (risks bugs) Automatic single-branch execution (no <code>break</code> needed) Unhandled Cases Silently falls through to <code>default</code> or exits Throws an <code>UnhandledMatchError</code> if no case matches <pre><code>&lt;?php
$statusCode = 404;
// 1. Direct value assignment from return
$message = match ($statusCode) {
    200, 201 =&gt; 'Success',
    400 =&gt; 'Bad Request',
    401, 403 =&gt; 'Unauthorized',
    404 =&gt; 'Resource Not Found',
    default =&gt; 'Internal Server Error',
};

// 2. Combining match with boolean expressions (Match on true)
$userRole = 'editor';
$isOwner = true;
$permission = match (true) {
    $userRole === 'admin' =&gt; 'full_access',
    $userRole === 'editor' &amp;&amp; $isOwner =&gt; 'edit_access',
    $userRole === 'editor' =&gt; 'read_access',
    default =&gt; 'no_access',
};
&gt;
</code></pre>
